{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1557080-feeding-in-hisil-and-fighting-spirits","id":1557080,"title":"Feeding in Hisil and fighting spirits","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-12-29T02:40:41-08:00","id":1557080,"title":"Feeding in Hisil and fighting spirits","content":"I'm not very expert or werewolf mechaincs butnI'd like to introduce some important character into a campaign of mine.<br /> I was wondering about two main topics for now:<br /> <br /> 1. What is the added value for an uratha to feed in Hisil rather than touching the core of a locus/verge?<br /> <br /> 2. How to properly represent the interaction/fight with Spirits into the hisil? Let's say a werewolf enter into a medieval church that he recognize as a locus and, for some reason, decide to cross the guntlet for feeding. I was thinking of having there Spirits of order and dominance represented by columns, Thrones, altars, maybe saint's statues(?). Woud these be in line and appropriate? Let's also say that, after a first observation and study the spirits decide to engage with the uratha. How would they interact with them initially? How would then a fight take place?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-29T04:09:57-08:00","id":1557085,"title":"","content":"Gargoyles keeping watch, saints who feel like they are looking into your soul for any sin, a stern nun with a ruler to enforce discipline, stained glass angels flying overhead and traversing the stained glass mosaics like rippling portals and a monk arising from the smoke of a flying thurible are some ideas that come to mind.<br /> <br /> If they are a spirit court, then it's all a matter of whether they keep to the order they enforce in their territory. They could try to guilt, discipline or intimidate them into respecting their rules, they could try to negotiate to promote their ideas in the material and more.<br /> <br /> Ultimately spirits want to increase the power of their ideas, by doing things like consuming similar ideas/spirits (or even ghosts, one might have consumed the ghost of a mudered priest) , promoting their ideas in the Material world, etc. They will absolutely throw down with werewolves if needed, but it's all about opportunity cost, spirits are monomaniacal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-29T04:15:29-08:00","id":1557087,"title":"","content":"Thanks. So the concept of columns and thrones as spirits doesn't fit? How would those example provided by you actually act/attack? <br /> Any insight about the first point also?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-29T04:30:36-08:00","id":1557089,"title":"","content":"The thrones and columns could totally work, depending on how people in the area feel about it. Looking at Spanish styled churches, such as those in the city center of Lima, you normally had carved wooden areas set up top near the top for the choir, as well as some in the back for the congregation to pray together or debate, maybe those could be animated as a type of spirit. If we look at Portuguese styled churches, like some the oldest ones in Rio de Janeiro, the columns usually had statues of saints, but nothing stops you from making them into nightmares fuel like the columns of Yahar'gul in <i>Bloodborne</i>, make them embody the guilt of the penitent.<br /> <br /> Regarding the first question, the biggest value I can think of is with the rite of the Sacred Hunt, gaining more power and Essence by regulating the Shadow in your territory. Remember, it doesn't need to destroy the spirit, just lay them low, which could be anything from sparing them at the end, to sabotaging their power base and more. You still need to pick your target deliberately, thinking about the image your pack is projecting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 12-29-2025, 08:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-29T13:06:11-08:00","id":1557101,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1557080-feeding-in-hisil-and-fighting-spirits#post1557080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. What is the added value for an uratha to feed in Hisil rather than touching the core of a locus/verge?</div> </div> </div> </div>Privacy from the material world, for one thing \u2014 there's less need to worry about the Herd finding out you were in a given place if you don't need to lay hands on a specific tree or window or standing stone to refuel.<br /> <br /> There's also lack of need to touch the core of what may be a fairly broad area \u2014 to make a very loose analogy to Mage, it's the difference between grabbing bits of tass and performing an oblation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-05T02:20:51-08:00","id":1557298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1557080-feeding-in-hisil-and-fighting-spirits?p=1557087#post1557087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks. So the concept of columns and thrones as spirits doesn't fit? How would those example provided by you actually act/attack?</div> </div> </div> </div>This depends a lot on the strength and nature of the spirits.<br /> <br /> A lot of things go on here. To begin with, it <i>somewhat</i> depends on how people see those objects. Spirits aren't simply the same objects found in the Material, but animated, and <i>the church itself</i> may be a spirit. So why is a particular object or architectural feature a standalone spirit and not a part of the church? Or even not there at all, the <b>Hisil</b> does not simply reflect everything. So things may be missing, some may be appendages to bigger entities, some entities may even manifest as &quot;swarms&quot; of sorts, seemingly distinct individuals that actually act as a whole. Some things are also &quot;just furniture&quot;, they're spirits or almost-spirit, but without a mind of their own, working effectively as objects and landscape as far as interaction goes.<br /> <br /> You have also the complexity of higher spirits. Those objects are Rank 1 spirits, simple-minded and just direct copies of the things they spawned from or those associated with their concept. From Rank 2 onward, spirits become more complex in concept and appearance, and diverge from mirroring things into being living metaphors for those things. Those spirits will probably stand out at once, and have more functional bodies for exploring the <b>Hisil</b>, like animal or human-like, or something weirder but obviously animated, like a machine.<br /> <br /> Finally, being a <i>locus</i> means the church also <i><b>attracts</b></i> spirits from elsewhere. Even if those are almost always related concepts, &quot;related&quot; here is something that can be stretched to some degree, and they're not born in the church to begin with. The <b>Hisil</b> of a church may be a lot more ecumenical, and even multi-religious, than the congregation that worship there. A church in an area where there's a lot of distinct religious communities could house spirits resembling elements from every religion in the area, and even be ruled by a powerful spirit related to another religion entirely. For the spirits this is not a concern. A church with a xenophobic congregation where the priest frequently gave heated speeches about destroying the heatens and heretics could house spirits of hate and violence, another that housed either the infirm or health professionals could have spirits of healing and/or disease. Again, not only spawned there, but also attracted from other places.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-06T11:32:55-08:00","id":1557347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1557080-feeding-in-hisil-and-fighting-spirits#post1557080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. What is the added value for an uratha to feed in Hisil rather than touching the core of a locus/verge?</div> </div> </div> </div>While I've gathered that you mean &quot;drawing Essence from a locus&quot; here, it is beneficial for Uratha to feed in the <i>Hisil </i>for more than one reason. With Rite of the Sacred Hunt, you can replenish Essence, help reinforce the predator-prey dynamics in your pack's territory, and find sustenance. It's hard for wolves to hunt in the city openly. Not every chronicle location has easy access to game, whether within city limits or outside of them. Packs of large canids hunting and killing things anywhere near civilization tend to draw attention eventually. It also becomes harder for werewolves to eat as their power grows, making spirits a tasty option.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}